---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who writes UmberLore, and the sourcing rule behind it: dates, attributions and locations come from the institution that actually holds the work."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
		<h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)] md:text-4xl">About UmberLore</h1>

		<div class="mt-7 max-w-[640px] text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/70">
			<p class="mb-4">
				UmberLore is about how art actually got made and what happened to it afterwards: the
				paintings and buildings, the pigments they were made from, the movements they get filed
				under, and the forgeries and thefts that keep turning the filing upside down.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Art history has a specific problem that made this site worth starting. Dates, attributions,
				dimensions and current locations get copied from blog to blog until the copy no longer
				matches the object. So the rule here is that those details come from the institution that
				holds the work, and the collection page is cited so you can check it yourself. Where
				scholars genuinely disagree, that gets said rather than smoothed over.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Umber is the brown earth pigment that comes in every paint box, raw or burnt. Lore is the
				accumulated telling. The name is meant literally: the material facts, plus the stories that
				built up around them.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4">
				One thing you won't find here is reproductions of work still under copyright. Modern and
				contemporary artists are written about freely, because discussing art is not the same as
				copying it, but the images alongside those pieces are portraits, buildings, or diagrams
				rather than the works themselves.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4 text-[var(--ink)]">
				This site is published by the {AUTHOR_NAME}.
			</p>
			<p class="m-0 text-[var(--ink)]">
				Questions, corrections, or press inquiries:
				<a href="mailto:contact@umberlore.com" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline">contact@umberlore.com</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
